### Migration Workflow API Testing

@MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress = https://localhost:5001
@workflowId = {{$guid}}

### 1. Start Simple Workflow (Default Settings)
POST {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/start-simple
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Start Custom Workflow
POST {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workflowId": "{{workflowId}}",
  "migrationRequest": {
    "collectionName": "Party",
    "targetTableName": "Customer",
    "batchSize": 100,
    "fromDate": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    "toDate": "2024-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  },
  "generateReconciliationReport": true,
  "performAnalysis": true
}

###

### 3. Start Workflow with Date Range
POST {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "migrationRequest": {
    "collectionName": "Party",
    "targetTableName": "Customer",
    "batchSize": 50,
    "fromDate": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    "toDate": "2024-06-30T23:59:59Z"
  },
  "generateReconciliationReport": true,
  "performAnalysis": true
}

###

### 4. Get Workflow Status
# Replace with actual workflow ID from previous responses
GET {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/status/your-workflow-id-here

###

### 5. Start Migration Only (No Reconciliation)
POST {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "migrationRequest": {
    "collectionName": "Party",
    "targetTableName": "Customer",
    "batchSize": 100
  },
  "generateReconciliationReport": false,
  "performAnalysis": false
}

###

### 6. Start Workflow with Large Batch Size
POST {{MigrationWorkflow_HostAddress}}/api/workflow/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "migrationRequest": {
    "collectionName": "Party",
    "targetTableName": "Customer",
    "batchSize": 500
  },
  "generateReconciliationReport": true,
  "performAnalysis": true
}

###

